import Mathlib.Tactic.Attr.Register

/-! # Equations of generated components

`component_equations` contains proved invocation equations emitted by the component compiler
(`component_equation`, `ConstructiveCryptography.DSL.Equations`). It is separate from the
default simp set: expanding a component is an explicit step, `simp only [component_equations]`
or `inline`. `component_definitions` holds the generated wrappers that `inline` unfolds to their
program constructors.
-/

/-- Proved equations for one invocation of a declared system or converter. -/
register_simp_attr component_equations

/-- The system and converter wrappers newly generated by the compiler, which `inline` expands
first. Bodies, pure functions and initial values are not registered. -/
register_simp_attr component_definitions
